## 📱 Supported Devices

| Device | Codename |
|---|---|
| OnePlus 8 | `instantnoodle` |
| OnePlus 8 Pro | `instantnoodlep` |
| OnePlus 8T | `kebab` |
| OnePlus 9R | `lemonades` |

---

## 🛣️ ROM Compatibility

| ROM Type | Status |
|---|---|
| Stock (OxygenOS / ColorOS-based) | ✅ Supported |
| Custom ROMs (Android 16 / A16) | 🚧 Coming soon |

---

## ✨ Features

- 🧠 **ReSukiSU** — manually integrated hooks for root management without a modified boot image
- 🥷 **SUSFS v2.2.0** — kernel-level root/module hiding for stronger detection resistance
- 📦 **Systemless AnyKernel3 installer** — OTA-friendly, compatible with autoflash apps
- 🐧 **Linux 4.19.325-cip132** base, rebased on `blu_spark`

---

## 📥 Installation

1. Make sure your bootloader is **unlocked** and you're on a **stock-based ROM/firmware** (custom ROM support is coming soon).
2. Download the latest flashable zip from the [XDA thread](https://xdaforums.com/t/kernel-4-19-op8-pro-t-tropsi_x-vx-x-custom-kernelsu.4794907/) or the repo's Releases page.
3. Flash the zip via **TWRP**, **OrangeFox**, or the **AnyKernel Flasher** app — over your current stock boot setup.
4. Reboot. First boot after flashing may take a little longer than usual.

💬 Join the [**Telegram group**](https://t.me/TropsiXKernel) for support, updates, and discussion.

---

## 📖 About

**Tropsi X** is a kernel for the OnePlus 8, 8 Pro, 8T, and 9R, with manually
integrated **ReSukiSU** hooks, **SUSFS v2.2.0**, a modern LLVM toolchain, and a
systemless AnyKernel3 installer. It's built for daily-driver stability first, with
performance and root access layered on top without breaking OTA compatibility.

> ⚠️ **Disclaimer:** Flashing a custom kernel carries risk of instability, bootloops,
> or other issues. You flash entirely at your own risk — the maintainer is not
> responsible for any damage to your device.

---

## 💖 Support Development

Custom ROM (A16) support is in the works — if you'd like to help speed that up,
donations go straight toward development time and testing devices.

**USDT (TRC20):**
```
TTL3HHUeyfDTXZ5RFqDr4Q379f8DXUJtjb
```

Every bit helps push custom ROM compatibility forward faster. 🙏

